{"conjecture": "EJ = K P_y (segment E–J equals segment K–P_y for every P_x on h1)", "reason": "1) VD = VE. Line j is parallel to tangent f, so angle(GE, j) = angle(GE, f) = angle CGE. Since CG = CE, angle CGE = angle CEG. Hence in triangle VDE the angles at D and E are equal, so VD = VE. 2) Intercept relation. V, D, H lie on j and V, E, J lie on g, with DE (the chord GE) parallel to HJ. By Thales, VE/VJ = VD/VH, which gives EJ·VD = VE·DH, i.e. EJ = DH·(VE/VD). With VD = VE this becomes EJ = DH. 3) DH = KP_y. Line e is perpendicular to j at D, and K lies on e. P_y K is parallel to j, and P_y H is parallel to h1, which is perpendicular to j. So K, D, H, P_y form a rectangle and DH = KP_y. Therefore EJ = KP_y for every P_x. Numerically EJ ≈ KP_y ≈ 11.345. The structural reason for this length: m is perpendicular to FP_x at P_x, and h1 is the vertex tangent, so P_y lies on the parabola with focus F and directrix e. Hence P_yF = P_yK, which checks numerically (P_yF ≈ 11.345). So the invariant chain is EJ = DH = KP_y = FP_y.", "closes_goal": true}
